{number: 160}
{title: O How I Love Jesus}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There [Ab] is a name I love to hear,
I love to sing its [Eb7] worth;
It [Ab] sounds like music in mine ear,
The [Db] sweetest [Ab] name [Eb7] on [Ab] earth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [Ab] how I love Jesus,
[Eb7] O how I love [Ab] Jesus,
O [Ab] how I love [Db] Jesus,
Because He [Ab] first [Eb7] loved [Ab] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
It [Ab] tells me of a Savior's love,
Who died to set me [Eb7] free;
It [Ab] tells me of His precious blood,
The [Db] sinner's [Ab] per-[Eb7] fect [Ab] plea.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
It [Ab] tells of One whose loving heart
Can feel my deepest [Eb7] woe;
Who [Ab] in each sorrow bears a part,
That [Db] none can [Ab] bear [Eb7] be-[Ab] low.
{end_of_verse}
